                <pb facs="0327" n="234" sameAs="frus:frus1935v04/pg234"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">714.18/31: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hanna</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName> [<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-02-27">undated</date>.]<lb/>[Received February 27, 1935—6:35
                        p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6. The following telegram has been sent to the Legation in Costa Rica: <pb
                        facs="0328" n="235" xml:id="pg235"/>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“February 27, 4 p.m. Your telegram February 22, 4 p.m. The Minister for
                            Foreign Affairs has expressed his pleasure with the prospective exchange
                            and by instruction of President Ubico has authorized me to inform you
                            that when the <hi rendition="#italic">agrément</hi> is requested as set
                            forth in your telegram this Government will immediately give a favorable
                            reply and will at the same time request the <hi rendition="#italic"
                                >agrément</hi> for Don Carlos Palma, former chief of protocol and
                            now attached to the Foreign Office, as Guatemalan Minister
                            Plenipotentiary to Costa Rica.</p>
                        <p>March 1st is an acceptable date for the exchange of telegrams. Repeated
                            to the Department.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanna</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
